{
 "title": "Duck portrait v2",
 "notes": [
  "The duck portrait repainted with the phase 4 process: values first, then flat colour in key, then light and form from the top right,",
  "then detail gathered at the head. The body is one flat yellow with a clipped shadow and light and a few hundred short feather strokes",
  "that follow the form; the wing is overlapping leaf stamps of varied size with a lighter second pass; a neck joins head and body;",
  "the beak has two mandibles and a shadow where it meets the head; the bokeh is bluer and the duck leaves room on the beak's side."
